1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,840
Around 1900, many Australians died of diseases they

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:07,680
caught from someone else, like pneumonia and tuberculosis.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,280
Today, most Australians die of diseases nobody can

4
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:15,520
catch: heart disease, dementia, stroke and lung cancer.

5
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:19,840
That's partly because vaccines, antibiotics and clean water

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,040
now prevent many deaths from infection, so more

7
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,520
people live long enough for these slower diseases

8
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,240
to develop.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:30,080
So if a disease isn't caught, what causes

10
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:30,480
it?

11
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,580
Start with the dividing line.

12
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,660
An infectious disease is caused by a pathogen,

13
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:40,340
like a bacterium or virus, invading and multiplying

14
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:41,540
in the body.

15
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:45,060
Many, but not all, can pass between hosts.

16
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:48,340
A non-infectious disease isn't caused by a pathogen,

17
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,940
so you can't catch it.

18
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:52,020
The test is the cause.

19
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:54,220
It isn't about how serious the disease is,

20
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:56,340
or whether genes are involved.

21
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:59,940
Cystic fibrosis is genetic, and it's still non-infectious,

22
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,860
because no pathogen causes it.

23
00:01:03,067 --> 00:01:04,746
So what does cause them?

24
00:01:05,227 --> 00:01:07,546
The causes fall into four groups.

25
00:01:07,787 --> 00:01:10,106
A genetic disease starts with a change in

26
00:01:10,187 --> 00:01:12,106
DNA that alters a protein.

27
00:01:12,587 --> 00:01:15,786
An environmental disease starts with something from outside

28
00:01:15,827 --> 00:01:17,546
the body that damages cells.

29
00:01:17,947 --> 00:01:20,746
A nutritional disease comes from too little, or

30
00:01:20,907 --> 00:01:22,626
too much, of a nutrient.

31
00:01:22,827 --> 00:01:26,146
And cancer is cells dividing out of control.

32
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:29,146
For each one, trace the same chain: the

33
00:01:29,227 --> 00:01:32,026
cause, what changes in the cells, and the

34
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:33,306
effect on the body.

35
00:01:34,534 --> 00:01:37,973
Start with a genetic disease, cystic fibrosis.

36
00:01:38,294 --> 00:01:41,013
Cells lining your airways make a protein called

37
00:01:41,174 --> 00:01:44,773
CFTR, from the CFTR gene.

38
00:01:45,094 --> 00:01:47,013
It's a channel in the cell membrane that

39
00:01:47,134 --> 00:01:50,453
lets chloride ions out onto the airway surface.

40
00:01:50,774 --> 00:01:53,733
Water follows the chloride by osmosis, so the

41
00:01:53,814 --> 00:01:56,773
mucus there stays thin and runny, and tiny

42
00:01:56,854 --> 00:01:59,493
hairs called cilia sweep it, with any trapped

43
00:01:59,574 --> 00:02:01,573
bacteria, up and out.

44
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:06,160
In cystic fibrosis, both copies of the CFTR

45
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,760
gene are altered.

46
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,720
The most common change removes one amino acid,

47
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,120
so the protein folds the wrong way, and

48
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,200
the cell breaks it down before it reaches

49
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,560
the membrane.

50
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:19,520
With too few channels, less chloride leaves the

51
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:22,400
cells, so less water follows.

52
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:24,720
The mucus dries out and turns thick and

53
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:25,840
sticky.

54
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,067
The cilia can't clear it, bacteria stay trapped,

55
00:02:29,093 --> 00:02:31,280
and the lungs get repeated infections.

56
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,540
Notice the order.

57
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:36,340
Thick mucus is the effect near the end

58
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:38,260
of the chain, not the cause.

59
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:41,420
The cause is the altered gene, then the

60
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:42,420
faulty protein.

61
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:46,340
And because cystic fibrosis needs two altered copies,

62
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,500
two healthy carriers can have a child with

63
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:48,740
it.

64
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:52,100
It runs in families, but it's inherited, not

65
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:52,820
caught.

66
00:02:54,034 --> 00:02:57,473
An environmental disease starts outside the body.

67
00:02:57,554 --> 00:03:00,353
Cutting engineered stone, once used for new kitchen

68
00:03:00,434 --> 00:03:03,793
benchtops, releases fine silica dust, which can be

69
00:03:03,874 --> 00:03:06,033
breathed deep into the lungs.

70
00:03:06,154 --> 00:03:08,513
Immune cells there take up the particles but

71
00:03:08,594 --> 00:03:11,073
can't break them down, and the damage leads

72
00:03:11,154 --> 00:03:12,673
to scar tissue.

73
00:03:12,834 --> 00:03:16,433
Scarred lungs are stiff, so breathing gets harder.

74
00:03:16,554 --> 00:03:18,113
That's silicosis.

75
00:03:18,194 --> 00:03:20,593
The dust caused it, and nobody caught it

76
00:03:20,714 --> 00:03:21,553
from anyone.

77
00:03:22,767 --> 00:03:25,726
Too little available iron, from a poor diet

78
00:03:25,807 --> 00:03:29,086
or poor absorption, can cause a nutritional deficiency

79
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:30,086
disease.

80
00:03:30,447 --> 00:03:33,246
Iron is part of haemoglobin, the protein in

81
00:03:33,327 --> 00:03:35,806
red blood cells that carries oxygen.

82
00:03:35,927 --> 00:03:38,366
With too little iron, the body makes less

83
00:03:38,407 --> 00:03:41,486
haemoglobin, so red blood cells come out smaller

84
00:03:41,607 --> 00:03:44,766
and paler, and the blood carries less oxygen.

85
00:03:44,887 --> 00:03:48,846
That's iron-deficiency anaemia, which can leave someone tired

86
00:03:48,967 --> 00:03:50,686
and short of breath.

87
00:03:50,807 --> 00:03:52,766
Too much of a nutrient can cause disease

88
00:03:52,847 --> 00:03:54,926
as well, and that's coming up soon.

89
00:03:56,134 --> 00:03:58,693
Cancer gets its own group, because it's defined

90
00:03:58,774 --> 00:04:01,093
by what the cells do, not by what

91
00:04:01,174 --> 00:04:02,133
started it.

92
00:04:02,454 --> 00:04:05,413
Genes normally control when a cell divides.

93
00:04:05,494 --> 00:04:07,973
When enough of those control genes are damaged,

94
00:04:08,054 --> 00:04:10,613
a cell keeps dividing, forms a lump called

95
00:04:10,694 --> 00:04:13,733
a tumour, and can invade nearby tissue.

96
00:04:13,814 --> 00:04:16,373
The damage can start in different ways.

97
00:04:16,454 --> 00:04:19,653
Melanoma, a skin cancer, is mainly triggered by

98
00:04:19,734 --> 00:04:22,413
ultraviolet light, so it's a cancer with an

99
00:04:22,454 --> 00:04:24,293
environmental trigger.

100
00:04:24,374 --> 00:04:26,693
Name the group first, then the trigger.

101
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:31,620
Real diseases often have several causes acting together.

102
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:36,300
Type 2 diabetes involves inherited genes, diet, activity

103
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:39,140
and age, all pushing the same way.

104
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:41,260
That's called multifactorial.

105
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:44,300
So when you classify a disease, name its

106
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:47,740
main contributing factor, then explain how that factor

107
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:49,100
changes cells.

108
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:51,660
Two exam questions.

109
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:52,700
First.

110
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:57,260
Three conditions are described on screen: goitre, Huntington's

111
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:59,260
disease and cervical cancer.

112
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,900
Classify each one into a group.

113
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:05,180
Then explain why a student who says cervical

114
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:07,420
cancer is infectious is wrong.

115
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:09,340
Pause here to answer.

116
00:05:19,767 --> 00:05:23,366
Goitre is nutritional: too little iodine, so the

117
00:05:23,447 --> 00:05:26,606
thyroid can't make enough hormone and enlarges.

118
00:05:26,887 --> 00:05:30,246
Huntington's is genetic: an altered gene leads to

119
00:05:30,327 --> 00:05:31,766
a harmful protein.

120
00:05:32,087 --> 00:05:34,886
Cervical cancer is a cancer, with an infectious

121
00:05:34,967 --> 00:05:35,766
trigger.

122
00:05:35,807 --> 00:05:38,086
The virus can pass between people, but the

123
00:05:38,167 --> 00:05:40,086
cancer itself can't.

124
00:05:40,167 --> 00:05:43,126
The classic mistake: a virus is involved, so

125
00:05:43,167 --> 00:05:44,486
it's infectious.

126
00:05:44,647 --> 00:05:47,286
Classify the disease, then name its trigger.

127
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,460
Second.

128
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:53,780
Familial hypercholesterolaemia is caused by an altered LDLR

129
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:54,820
gene.

130
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:57,540
Normally, this gene codes for a receptor on

131
00:05:57,620 --> 00:06:00,500
liver cells that removes LDL cholesterol from the

132
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:01,460
blood.

133
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,940
Explain how the altered gene can lead to

134
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:05,300
heart disease.

135
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:06,740
Pause here to answer.

136
00:06:17,167 --> 00:06:20,686
The altered gene means fewer working LDL receptors

137
00:06:20,767 --> 00:06:21,886
on liver cells.

138
00:06:22,127 --> 00:06:25,166
So the liver removes less LDL, and LDL

139
00:06:25,247 --> 00:06:27,406
cholesterol builds up in the blood.

140
00:06:27,727 --> 00:06:31,486
Over years it's deposited in artery walls, narrowing

141
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:33,566
the arteries that supply the heart.

142
00:06:33,887 --> 00:06:37,446
That's gene, protein, cells, body.

143
00:06:37,807 --> 00:06:40,686
The classic mistake is calling it nutritional because

144
00:06:40,767 --> 00:06:43,246
fatty food raises cholesterol.

145
00:06:43,287 --> 00:06:45,486
Diet can add to it, but the cause

146
00:06:45,567 --> 00:06:46,446
is the gene.

147
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:50,786
So for any disease, first ask: is it

148
00:06:50,867 --> 00:06:52,226
caused by a pathogen?

149
00:06:52,707 --> 00:06:55,266
If not, ask what kind of disease it

150
00:06:55,427 --> 00:06:59,266
is: genetic, environmental, nutritional, or cancer.

151
00:06:59,907 --> 00:07:02,866
Then ask what factor contributed, and trace the

152
00:07:02,947 --> 00:07:03,906
chain to the body.

153
00:07:04,547 --> 00:07:08,466
Next: how environmental exposures cause disease.

154
00:07:09,667 --> 00:07:11,106
Here are the key notes.

155
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:13,266
Pause the video if you need more time

156
00:07:13,347 --> 00:07:14,146
to copy them.
